<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net9.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational" Version="9.0.14" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Agents.AI.OpenAI" Version="1.0.0-rc2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Azure.AI.OpenAI" Version="2.8.0-beta.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenAI" Version="2.8.0" />
    <!--
      PINNED, and the version ceiling is load-bearing. Do not bump without reading this.

      The `Anthropic` package is first-party from v10 onward (3.x and below were the community
      tryAGI build, now `tryAGI.Anthropic`). Its constraint here is its Microsoft.Extensions.AI
      dependency, NOT its own API:

        Anthropic 12.9.0  -> Microsoft.Extensions.AI.Abstractions 10.2.0  (unifies to the 10.3.0
                             Microsoft.Agents.AI.OpenAI already brings; nothing else moves)
        Anthropic 12.10.0 -> Microsoft.Extensions.AI.Abstractions 10.4.0  (BREAKS THE BUILD, below)

      Abstractions 10.4.0 REMOVED seven public types (FunctionApproval{Request,Response}Content,
      McpServerToolApproval{Request,Response}Content, UserInput{Request,Response}Content,
      IToolReductionStrategy). Microsoft.Agents.AI.Workflows 1.0.0-rc2 was compiled against 10.3.0
      and still references them from Specialized.AIAgentHostExecutor.ConfigureUserInputHandling.
      Nothing in this solution names that executor, but InProcessExecution.RunStreamingAsync
      instantiates it to host an AIAgent — which is exactly what every room step
      (EditRoom/GraphicsRoom/ColorGradeRoom) does. So a newer Anthropic throws
      TypeLoadException at run time in all 13 room tests, while `dotnet build` passes clean.

      Lifting the ceiling means upgrading the whole Microsoft.Agents.AI family (rc2 -> 1.22.0),
      which in turn requires OpenAI 2.8.0 -> 2.13.0 and a matching Azure.AI.OpenAI. That is a
      separate piece of work, not a version bump.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Anthropic" Version="12.9.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.DataProtection.Abstractions" Version="9.0.14" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Binder" Version="9.0.9" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
